 ## Confusion points and common mistakes
 
+- **MultiAgentV2 handoff is provider-aware; Copilot is plaintext.** `ProviderCapabilities::encrypted_inter_agent_messages` defaults to `true`, while `CopilotModelProvider::capabilities()` explicitly returns `false`. `core/src/tools/spec_plan.rs::add_collaboration_tools` derives one `V2MessageEncoding` and passes it to the spawn/send/follow-up schemas and handlers, so Copilot exposes ordinary string messages and constructs truthful `InterAgentCommunication::new(...)` input; encryption-capable providers retain `encrypted_content` plus `new_encrypted(...)`. Do not special-case only the schema or only runtime — they must use the same encoding. V2 `wait_agent(task_name=...)` subscribes to the exact target status before its first `borrow_and_update()` read, so an already-final child returns immediately without a race; omitted `task_name` keeps mailbox-wide behavior. The rebase guard is `just test -p codex-invariant-tests --test multi_agent_v2_handoff`; see patch-surface invariants 76–77 and their §15 replant recipes.
+
 - `CopilotHeaderSource::inject()` is the session-header seam. If Copilot headers are missing, start there.
 - `ResponsesClient::pre_send_hook` is the per-request mutation seam. `core::copilot_transport::build_copilot_client(...)` owns the shared Copilot hook.
 - `supports_websockets=false` on the built-in Copilot provider is intentional in v6.
