+## v0.141.0-copilot-api.3 V2 handoff and exact-wait regressions (2026-07-14)
+
+Introduced in `v0.141.0-copilot-api.3`; fixed in the
+`v0.141.0-copilot-api.4` source candidate. Publication and installation of
+`.4` remain lead/operator-owned.
+
+- **Opaque Copilot child handoff:** MultiAgentV2 exposed `encrypted_content`
+  schemas and always constructed encrypted `agent_message` payloads even though
+  the Copilot Responses transport cannot supply the provider-native encrypted
+  handoff token. Copilot children therefore received opaque/unusable handoff
+  input. `.4` adds the general
+  `ProviderCapabilities::encrypted_inter_agent_messages` capability, defaults
+  capable providers to encrypted behavior, explicitly marks Copilot plaintext,
+  and derives one encoding for spawn/send/follow-up schema plus runtime
+  construction. V1 and encryption-capable providers remain unchanged.
+- **Already-final exact wait:** V2 `wait_agent` only waited on aggregate mailbox
+  activity and had no exact target. A child that reached a final state before
+  the wait started could leave the parent waiting until timeout. `.4` adds the
+  optional `task_name` branch and subscribes to the target's Tokio status watch
+  before reading its current value, covering completion before setup, during
+  setup, and afterward without a check/subscribe gap. Targetless V2 behavior is
+  unchanged.
+- **Required evidence:** retain the focused provider-schema/runtime tests, the
+  focused exact-wait tests (already-final, future final, unrelated completion,
