+### MultiAgentV2 behavior
+
+Copilot does not provide the encrypted inter-agent handoff token expected by
+other providers. The fork therefore derives one provider capability while
+planning V2 tools: Copilot spawn/send/follow-up schemas use plaintext strings
+and runtime constructs plaintext `agent_message/input_text`; capable providers
+keep `encrypted_content`. Schema and runtime must never be changed separately.
+
+For an exact child completion, call V2 `wait_agent` with `task_name`. The wait
+subscribes to that target before reading its current status, so already-final
+and future-final children use the same race-free path. Leave `task_name` absent
+for the existing mailbox-wide wait. Operational containment is
+`-c features.multi_agent_v2=false`; the immutable `.3` rollback procedure and
+pins are in [Install Guide](install.md#roll-back-from-the-4-v2-change).
